// t-seq-01: an abort(..) that fires while a try-body step's errors drain
// loses to the try's jump: the aborted run enters its with body.
//
// A try-body step that raises two errors in one cycle gets the second one
// a cycle later (node/error.rs:603-604, deliver_error's set_var fallback),
// so the jump catch runs `pc <- S_with` in that later cycle
// (node/error.rs:339) without looking at the machine handler. An abort
// firing in that cycle also runs the machine catch's `pc <- Idle`; the
// runtime requeues the second of the two pc writes (graphix-rt/src/gx.rs
// push_var_event), so pc goes S1 (with body), Idle, then the with body's
// own `pc <- S2` (join) lands after Idle and resumes the dead run from
// idle under the next run's trigger snapshot.
//
// Run 1 (c = 1) fails both `?` in the cycle it enters; the abort fires at
// step 3, the cycle the second error is delivered. Run 2 (c = 5) cannot
// fail.
//
// command: timeout -s KILL 30 graphix --no-cache design/review-2026-10-05/repro/t-seq-01.gx
//          (--no-fusion, GRAPHIX_PAR=off|force and a warm image print the
//          same; graphix-fuzz check: AGREE, both engines run one machine)
//
// expected: (5, 10). design/seq_blocks.md §9: an abort is silent and a try
//   around the current step is not taken, so run 1 ends at step 3 and run 2
//   completes. The same program with one failing `?` (`let b = c;`) prints
//   (5, 10).
// observed (HEAD c722befe, debug build): (5, -1) and nothing else: run 1's
//   fallback paired with run 2's c, and run 2's own result lost.
//   GRAPHIX_DBG_VARS=1 shows pc <- "S1" and pc <- "Idle" written in the
//   abort cycle, later pc <- "S2" delivered after "Idle".
let step = 0;
step <- select step { n if n < 30 => n + 1, _ => never() };
let go = select step { 1 | 5 => step, _ => never() };
let r = seq let c = go; abort(select step { 3 => true, _ => never() }) {
  let v = try {
    {
      let a = (select c { 1 => error(`A), n => n })?;
      let b = (select c { 1 => error(`B), n => n })?;
      a + b
    }
  } with(e) {
    -1
  };
  (c, v)
};
sys::exit(sys::time::after_idle(duration:300.ms, 0));
r
